6,80,80,37,67,52,70,44,85,80,37,0],"nar":[{"lap":1,"text":"The race was held over 90 laps of the Circuit Mont-Tremblant, taking place in sunny conditions, with the Ferrari of Chris Amon leading straight from the off, with Jo Siffert chasing him.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":7},{"lap":29,"text":"An oil leak accounted for Siffert, on lap 29, and so Rindt was second, although he too retired shortly afterwards with an engine failure.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":14},{"lap":73,"text":"While all this was going on, Amon seemed to have everything under control for the first 72 laps of the race, however, on the 73rd lap, his legendary bad luck struck when his Ferrari's transmission failed.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":7},{"lap":90,"text":"On lap 14, Hill managed pass Gurney, and 12 laps later, the American dropped away with a broken radiator.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":3},{"lap":90,"text":"A few laps later (lap 71), the Matra of Servoz-Gavin had spun out and Hill was back up to fifth.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":8},{"lap":90,"text":"Hulme won in a time of 2hr 27.11.2mins., averaging a speed of 97.799 mph, and was a full lap ahead of his team-mate.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":0}]}